From f98aaddd46476b732db8f4e3f9d31409d22391c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Lopez <plopez@unc.edu.ar>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:28:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read Gadget-4 binary snapshots (tries the Gadget-2 header
 first, then Gadget-4)

- Gadget_header::readHeaderBlock(): reads the header block of a binary
  snapshot trying the Gadget-1/2 header (256 bytes) first and then the
  default Gadget-4 header (24*N+48 bytes); stops with an error only if
  none matches. The header is stored in the Gadget-2 layout.
- Used in all the places that read binary Gadget headers (first file,
  particle count of multi-file snapshots, per-file reading, density file
  header info), formats 1 and 2.
- Fix reading of snapshots with opposite endianness (block sizes were not
  byte-swapped before seeking).
- README: supported Gadget formats.

Tested against an HDF5 reference with identical particles: Gadget-2 and
Gadget-4 headers, formats 1 and 2, float and double positions, 64-bit IDs,
multi-file snapshots and big-endian files all give identical density and
velocity fields. Gadget-2 results are unchanged with respect to the
previous code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
